---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';

/**
 * /terms
 *
 * The two clauses that carry real weight here are accuracy and booking. This
 * guide publishes bus times, ticket prices, opening hours and road conditions
 * for a mountain in Zhejiang, all of which move; and every booking a reader
 * makes happens on somebody else's system. Both are stated early rather than
 * buried, because a reader who is misled by a timetable will not care what
 * clause 11 said.
 */
const SECTIONS = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', label: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'accepting-these-terms', label: 'Accepting these terms' },
  { id: 'what-this-site-is', label: 'What this site is' },
  { id: 'accuracy', label: 'Accuracy' },
  { id: 'booking', label: 'Booking and third parties' },
  { id: 'money', label: 'How we make money' },
  { id: 'our-content', label: 'Our content' },
  { id: 'your-content', label: 'Your content' },
  { id: 'acceptable-use', label: 'Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'availability', label: 'Availability' },
  { id: 'liability', label: 'Liability' },
  { id: 'law', label: 'Governing law' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms"
  seoTitle="Terms of use · Visit Moganshan"
  description="The terms on which Visit Moganshan is published: what the guide is, what it is not, how bookings with third parties work and where liability sits."
  standfirst="Plain terms for a guide that publishes timetables, prices and opening hours for a mountain where all three change. Read the accuracy and booking sections if you read nothing else."
  updated="2026-08-05"
  sections={SECTIONS}
>
  <h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Visit Moganshan is published by BeyondBorder Group Ltd, registered in Hong Kong. In these terms,
    "we", "us" and "our" mean that company, "the site" means visitmoganshan.com and everything served
    from it, and "you" means anyone using it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="accepting-these-terms">Accepting these terms</h2>
  <p>
    Using the site means you accept these terms. If you do not accept them, please stop using the
    site. They work alongside our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>, our
    <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a> and, if you send us photographs or words for publication,
    our <a href="/user-generated-content">user generated content terms</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-this-site-is">What this site is</h2>
  <p>
    An independent travel guide to Moganshan and the surrounding part of Deqing county: how to get
    there, where to stay, what there is to do and when to come. It is editorial information, freely
    published for planning purposes.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is not a travel agency, a tour operator, a booking agent or a licensed adviser of any kind. We
    do not sell transport, accommodation, tickets or insurance, we hold no funds on your behalf, and
    we are not party to any contract you enter with a hotel, host, operator or carrier.
  </p>

  <h2 id="accuracy">Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We research every page, we date every page, and we correct them when we learn they are wrong.
    That is a serious commitment and it is still not a guarantee. Bus and train times change without
    notice. Ticket prices rise. Trails close for maintenance, weather or fire risk. Hotels change
    hands, change policy and change their attitude to foreign passports. Roads up the mountain close
    in snow and at peak holiday periods.
  </p>
  <p>
    So treat the site as a well researched starting point and confirm anything your trip actually
    depends on with the operator, the property or the official source before you rely on it. That
    goes double for last transport of the day, entry requirements, closing dates and anything
    involving a fixed connection.
  </p>
  <p>
    Found something wrong? Tell us. Corrections from readers are the fastest way this guide improves,
    and we act on them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="booking">Booking and third parties</h2>
  <p>
    When you follow a link from this site to a hotel, a host, a rail or flight booking system, a
    ticketing platform or a map service, you leave our site and deal directly with that company under
    its own terms and its own privacy policy. Your contract is with them. Payment, confirmation,
    changes, cancellation, refunds and complaints are matters between you and them, and we have no
    ability to intervene.
  </p>
  <p>
    We choose the properties and operators we write about on editorial grounds, but we do not
    inspect, licence, insure or supervise any of them, and their appearance on this site is not a
    warranty about their conduct or their safety.
  </p>

  <h2 id="money">How we make money</h2>
  <p>
    Some links on this site may earn us a commission if you book through them, at no additional cost
    to you. Commission never buys a place in a ranking, never buys a favourable line, and never
    prevents us from writing that somewhere is not worth the money. Where a commercial relationship
    exists, we disclose it. The full statement of how the site is funded is on the
    <a href="/about">About page</a>, and it is the sentence we would most like you to hold us to.
  </p>
  <p>
    Specifically: every rates link on this site, including every "Check dates" link in the property
    listings, goes to Trip.com through a tracked path and earns us a commission if you book. You pay
    the same price you would pay going to Trip.com directly. It changes nothing about which
    properties are listed or in what order, and there is no field in the data behind those listings
    that could promote one property over another. What that pays for and what it does not buy is set
    out at <a href="/plan/disclosure">how this site is funded</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing on a property card is written by us. The photographs, the review scores and the prices
    are Trip.com's, captured from their listing rather than composed here, and "Check dates" opens
    Trip.com in a new tab.
  </p>

  <h2 id="our-content">Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The text, photographs, maps, illustrations, design, code and marks on this site belong to
    BeyondBorder Group Ltd or to our licensors, and are protected by copyright and trade mark law.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are welcome to read the site, print pages for your own trip, and quote a short extract with
    attribution and a link back. You may not republish substantial parts of the guide, copy its
    structure or copy wholesale, scrape it for a competing directory, use our photographs or marks
    commercially, or feed it into a product or dataset that reproduces it, without our written
    permission. Ask us. We say yes more often than you would expect.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-content">Your content</h2>
  <p>
    If you send us a photograph, a correction, a review or any other material for publication, the
    <a href="/user-generated-content">user generated content terms</a> apply to it. In short: it
    stays yours, you give us permission to publish it, and you confirm it is genuinely yours to give.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use the site unlawfully, or in a way that breaks the law of your own country or of China;</li>
    <li>
      scrape, crawl at a rate that degrades service, or attempt to bypass any technical measure
      protecting the site;
    </li>
    <li>attempt to gain access to systems, accounts or data that are not yours;</li>
    <li>
      introduce malware, or use the site to distribute it, or attack its availability for others; or
    </li>
    <li>impersonate us, or present the guide as your own work or as endorsing a business.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may block access where we reasonably believe any of the above is happening.</p>

  <h2 id="availability">Availability</h2>
  <p>
    We publish this site as a static build and we work hard to keep it fast and reachable, including
    from inside mainland China. We still cannot promise it will always be available, or reachable
    from every network, and we may change, move or withdraw any page at any time. Nothing here is a
    commitment to keep a particular page online forever.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">Liability</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided as it is. To the fullest extent the law allows, we exclude the implied
    warranties and conditions that would otherwise apply to it, including as to accuracy,
    completeness, fitness for a particular purpose and uninterrupted availability.
  </p>
  <p>
    We are not liable for loss or damage arising from your use of the site or from reliance on
    anything published here, including missed transport, cancelled or unsatisfactory accommodation,
    closed attractions, additional costs, lost time or lost enjoyment, or from your dealings with any
    third party you found through us.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence,
    for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be limited.
    Where liability cannot be excluded, it is limited to the amount you have paid us, which for a
    reader of this guide is nothing.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law">Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, and the
    courts of Hong Kong have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them. If you are a
    consumer resident elsewhere, this does not deprive you of the protection of mandatory consumer
    rules in your own country.
  </p>
  <p>
    If any part of these terms is found to be unenforceable, the rest stays in force. If we do not
    enforce a term straight away, we have not given it up.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We update these terms from time to time. The date at the top of the page is the date of the
    current version, and using the site after a change means you accept the version then published.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms, permission requests and rights complaints go to
    <a href="mailto:hello@visitmoganshan.com">hello@visitmoganshan.com</a>. Everything else is on the
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
